    "title": "New class demographics essay change - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Skye Bulman ,\n1 days ago Wellesley’s class of 2029 shows little demographic changes from last year’s class, which had the lowest Black and Latina enrollments in the last decade. The News previously reported a significant drop in the percentage of enrolled African American students in the Class of 2028, from 9% in the previous year down to 5% last fall. That percentage has remained consistent for the Class of 2029, despite a change in the supplemental essay prompt. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
